Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/pds/tif_pdsdirread.c
Line: 400
Function: TIFFFetchData
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: When memory-mapped, the code checks if (dir->tdir_offset + cc > tif->tif_size) before memcpy. The addition is performed in 32-bit unsigned arithmetic (uint32_t + tsize_t), which can wrap and bypass the bound check. This can lead to memcpy reading past the end of the mapped file buffer.

